{start_of_verse: verse 1}
[C]By the shattered calls of a mother's arms
All swept-inside like the rosary
[F]That fell away when her girlish charms
Cried out to take on motherhood
[C]She waits by the windowsill
All wrapped in white and puzzling
[F]What happened to the child inside?
Who ran the streets and the days at night...

[C]She says, "Nothing seems the same."
And, "I can't change a thing."
[F]"My body's like a wave, breaking to the sea."
[C]She says, "Everything seems strange."
Locked behind the years
[F]But life is ours to find, in the days at night

{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: verse 2}
[C]There passes a stranger every eve
Who walks himself on a silver-leash
[F]And in his head, the worlds asleep
Or, so the wrinkles in his hands believe
[C]When he was young, he had a dream
To be a star, on the movie-screen
[F]Now it all seems a silly lie
As he walks alone
And, the days on fire

[C]He says, "Nothing seems the same."
And, "I can't feel a thing."
[F]"My bodies like a wave, caving in on me"
[C]He says, "Everything seems strange."
Holding back the tears
[F]And he smiles just like a child
In the days at night

{end_of_verse}
